,\n      \"title\": null,\n      \"index\": 1,\n      \"start_position\": 28,\n      \"end_position\": 13811,\n      \"word_count\": 2443,\n      \"estimated_duration_minutes\": 16.286666666666665,\n      \"confidence\": \"medium\",\n      \"children\": [],\n      \"characters_present\": [\n        \"Prince Prospero\",\n        \"The masked figure (Red Death)\"\n      ],\n      \"summary\": \"The chapter opens with the devastation of the 'Red Death' plague, which kills swiftly with bleeding pores and scarlet stains, isolating victims from society. Prince Prospero, in defiance, retreats with a thousand courtiers to his sealed, abbey-like castle, where he provides endless entertainment and ignores the outside horror. Months later, he hosts a lavish masked ball in seven uniquely colored rooms, each with stained-glass windows matching their hue, culminating in a black chamber with blood-red panes and a massive ebony clock that chimes hourly, halting all merriment. During the midnight chime, a mysterious figure appears dressed as the Red Death itself—dripping in blood and wearing a corpse-like mask—causing terror and outrage. The prince, enraged, pursues the figure through all seven rooms with a dagger, but the figure turns in the black chamber, and the prince collapses dead. The revelers rush in, only to find the mask and robes empty, realizing the plague has infiltrated their sanctuary, and one by one, they die as the clock stops and darkness claims all.\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"characters\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"char_the_prince_prospero_d85685e9\",\n      \"canonical_name\": \"the Prince Prospero\",\n      \"aliases\": [],\n      \"role\": null,\n      \"appearance\": null,\n      \"personality\": null,\n      \"voice_guidance\": null,\n      \"descriptions\": [],\n      \"relationships\": {},\n      \"evidence\": [],\n      \"voice_notes\": null,\n      \"first_appearance_chapter\": 1,\n      \"mention_count\": 3,\n      \"confidence\": \"high\",\n      \"is_narrator